  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Trust Fund for the Multilateral Fund for the Implementation of the Montreal Protocol on Substances that Deplete the Ozone Layer 2024-2026</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The activity aims at the reduction of ozone depleting substances in the atmosphere and at prevention of the production and use of ozone depleting gasses and substances. It concerns phasing out of hydrochlorofluorocarbons (HCFCs) and the first reduction step for hydrofluorocarbons (HFCs) (Kigali) . In addition, attention for PFAS and trifluoroacetic acid (TFA) as degradation products of refrigerants. Progress needs to be made regarding substances that (or various Very Short-Lived Substances - VSLS) are not yet regulated. The Multilateral Fund was established by the Second Meeting of the Parties to the Montreal Protocol (London, June 1990) and began its operation in 1991. The main objective of the Fund is to assist developing country parties to the Montreal Protocol whose annual level of consumption of the ozone depleting substances (ODS) chlorofluorocarbons (CFCs) and halons is less than 0.3 kilograms per capita to comply with the control measures of the Protocol. Currently, 147 of the 197 Parties to the MP meet these criteria.</narrative>
  </description>
